@page "/students"

<PageTitle>For Students - Utkeern</PageTitle>

<section class="students-hero">
    <div class="students-hero-content">
        <h1>For Students</h1>
        <p>Educational resources and usage guidelines for heritage learning</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <SectionHeader Title="Educational Resources" />

        <div class="guidelines-section">
            <h2>How to Use Utkeern Resources</h2>
            <p>
                We're committed to making heritage education accessible to students worldwide. All resources on Utkeern 
                are provided with clear usage guidelines to support your academic and creative projects.
            </p>

            <div class="guidelines-cards">
                <GuidelineCard 
                    Icon="📚"
                    Title="Academic Projects"
                    Description="Use heritage images and articles for essays, research papers, presentations, and theses. Always cite the source." />
                
                <GuidelineCard 
                    Icon="🎨"
                    Title="Creative Work"
                    Description="Incorporate heritage inspiration into artwork, design projects, and creative assignments with proper attribution." />
                
                <GuidelineCard 
                    Icon="📖"
                    Title="Learning & Study"
                    Description="Explore articles and collections for personal learning, exam preparation, and cultural understanding." />
                
                <GuidelineCard 
                    Icon="📊"
                    Title="Presentations"
                    Description="Create compelling educational presentations using our collection with appropriate citations." />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="heritage-divider"></div>

<section class="content alt">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <h2>Usage Rules & License</h2>

        <div class="usage-rules">
            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">1</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>Attribution Required</h4>
                    <p>
                        Always credit "Utkeern" as the source. Format: "Image from Utkeern - Indian Heritage Archive" 
                        or similar attribution.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">2</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>Non-Commercial Use</h4>
                    <p>
                        Educational use is encouraged. Commercial use requires explicit permission. Contact us for 
                        licensing inquiries.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">3</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>No Modification Without Permission</h4>
                    <p>
                        Do not alter, modify, or create derivatives without permission. Preserve the integrity of 
                        cultural heritage materials.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">4</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>Respect Cultural Context</h4>
                    <p>
                        Present heritage materials respectfully within their cultural and historical context. Avoid 
                        misrepresentation.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">5</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>Share & Distribute</h4>
                    <p>
                        Share resources with fellow students and educators. Help spread awareness of heritage preservation 
                        efforts.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rule">
                <div class="rule-number">6</div>
                <div class="rule-content">
                    <h4>Provide Feedback</h4>
                    <p>
                        Help us improve. Share your experiences, suggest new resources, and contribute your own research 
                        and insights.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="heritage-divider"></div>

<section class="content">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <SectionHeader Title="Research & Citation Guide" />

        <div class="citation-guide">
            <div class="citation-example">
                <h4>How to Cite Utkeern Images</h4>
                <p class="example-text">
                    Author. "Image Title." Utkeern - Indian Heritage Archive. Accessed [Date]. 
                    https://utkeern.com/gallery
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="citation-example">
                <h4>How to Cite Utkeern Articles</h4>
                <p class="example-text">
                    Author. "Article Title." Utkeern - Indian Heritage Archive. [Date]. 
                    https://utkeern.com/research
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="citation-example">
                <h4>Bibliography Format</h4>
                <p class="example-text">
                    Utkeern - Indian Heritage Archive. https://utkeern.com. Accessed [Date]. 
                    [Provide specific images or articles used in square brackets]
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="help-text">
            Need help with citations? Check your school's preferred citation style (MLA, APA, Chicago, etc.) 
            and adapt the examples above accordingly.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content alt">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <SectionHeader Title="Student Community" />

        <div class="community-section">
            <h3>Join the Heritage Learning Community</h3>
            <p>
                Connect with fellow students, share your projects, ask questions, and collaborate on heritage research. 
                Our community forum is a space for learners to explore Indian culture together.
            </p>
            
            <div class="community-links">
                <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary">Join Community</a>
                <a href="#" class="btn btn-secondary">Submit Your Project</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-section">
            <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can I use these images in my school project?</summary>
                <p>Yes! Educational use is encouraged. Just remember to cite Utkeern as the source.</p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Do I need permission to use the images?</summary>
                <p>
                    For non-commercial educational use, no special permission is needed. For commercial or derivative uses, 
                    please contact us.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Can I include images in my published thesis?</summary>
                <p>Yes, for academic theses with proper citations. Contact us if you need high-resolution versions.</p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>How do I contribute my own research?</summary>
                <p>
                    We welcome student research and articles. Submit your work through our contribution guidelines 
                    for review.
                </p>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
                <summary>Is there support for group projects?</summary>
                <p>
                    Absolutely! Utkeern resources work great for group presentations and collaborative projects. 
                    Share these links with your teammates.
                </p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

